<title>USA: Children's Broadcasting buys radio license.</title>
<headline>Children's Broadcasting buys radio license.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Children's Broadcasting Corp said Friday it acquired the radio broadcast license of WAUR-AM 930 from Nelson Broadcasting in a deal valued at $3.9 million.</p>
<p>A company spokeswoman said the station, based in Sandwich, Ill., serves the metropolitan Chicago area.</p>
<p>Children's Broadcasting produces radio programming for children and families through its Radio AAHS network.</p>
<p>Its shares were trading up 1/8 Friday at 5-1/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
